        "problem": "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6}).$",
        "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-6)!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6!}{1!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot \\cancel{6!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{6!}} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
